Z||000010||PaUL||07-15-99||03:32 PM||||My opinion on the exhaust wrap is that it serves no purpose other than making your arms itch when working on the engine. I installed the wrap on my exhaust about 5 years ago and completely removed it last week. To me it made no noticable difference in underhood heat reduction. It also deteriorates with age becoming brittle and dusty. The dust gets in your eyes and lungs and is very irritating. 
Z||000011||mwbackus||07-16-99||12:27 PM||||If you are using a Hypertech Streetrunner rather than the Thermomaster, you would still be running in open loop at those temperatures.  The symtoms you describe would indicate that this is the case.  The dust from exhaust wraps could very likely contain asbestos.  Inhalation of even slight amounts of asbestos dust is VERY dangerous to ones health.
